WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.036 line:0%
-Benedict, since you've been
in so many fantastic movies

00:00:03.036 --> 00:00:05.338 line:0%
spanning so many genres,
I thought it'd be fun

00:00:05.338 --> 00:00:07.506 line:0%
if we put your movie knowledge
to the test.

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:11.210 line:0%
It is time for "A to Z."

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:13.612 line:0%
-♪ A to Z ♪

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:15.314 line:0%
♪ A to Z ♪

00:00:15.314 --> 00:00:17.917 line:0%
-All right.
You probably call it "A to Zed."

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:19.619 line:0%
I'm assuming

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:21.320 line:0%
-I could do "Z."
It's fine.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:23.490 line:0%
-Here's how it'll work.
You're very nice.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.691 line:0%
You and I are going to
have a conversation

00:00:25.691 --> 00:00:27.326 line:0%
about our favorite movies,

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.862 line:0%
but the catch is that each time
one of us brings up a new one,

00:00:29.862 --> 00:00:33.099 line:0%
the title has to start with
the next letter of the alphabet.

00:00:33.099 --> 00:00:34.667 line:0%
We're going to go back and forth

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.171 line:0%
and see if we can get
all the way from A to Z.

00:00:38.171 --> 00:00:39.839 line:0%
You ready?
-Okay. Okay.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.908 line:0%
-Benedict, it's been such
a crazy year in quarantine.

00:00:42.908 --> 00:00:46.812 line:0%
I've watched nonstop movies,
and it's the best because

00:00:46.812 --> 00:00:50.750 line:0%
I obviously I had to start
with "Animal House."

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.686 line:0%
-Yeah, yeah, I mean, you know,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.120 line:0%
and the thing about
"Animal House"

00:00:55.120 --> 00:00:57.923 line:0%
is how many "Bad Boys" there are
in that "Animal House."

00:00:57.923 --> 00:01:00.493 line:0%
-Yeah, yeah.
I mean, it reminded me

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:02.462 line:0%
of "Chaplin" a little bit
because he was a bad boy,

00:01:02.462 --> 00:01:05.265 line:0%
because he didn't speak
in any of his movies, did he?

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.200 line:0%
Yeah?
-Yeah, you're right.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.468 line:0%
You're right there.
Well, "Don't Look Now,"

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:12.671 line:0%
but, you know...
-Of course.

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:13.973 line:0%
I mean, did they sing?

00:01:13.973 --> 00:01:16.141 line:0%
'Cause they sang
in "Ever After."

00:01:16.141 --> 00:01:17.643 line:0%
Drew Barrymore...
-They did.

00:01:17.643 --> 00:01:20.613 line:0%
-Yeah, they sang a little bit.
-That's right.

00:01:20.613 --> 00:01:25.218 line:0%
But she was in "Forever Young,"
wasn't she?

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.252 line:0%
Maybe she wasn't.
-Yeah, well, no,

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:28.354 line:0%
she was in "Fever Pitch"
with me,

00:01:28.354 --> 00:01:31.090 line:0%
the American version.
-That's right. That's right.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:34.627 line:0%
She was not in "Goodfellas."
-No.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:38.264 line:0%
Or "High Society."
-No. And she wasn't in, um...

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.837 line:0%
"I'll Fly Away."
Is that a movie?

00:01:44.837 --> 00:01:48.575 line:0%
-Hey, have you seen
"Jurassic Park"?

00:01:48.575 --> 00:01:51.143 line:0%
I saw "Jurassic Park."
It was a double feature.

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:53.612 line:0%
I saw "Jurassic Park"
and then "Karate Kid,"

00:01:53.612 --> 00:01:54.780 line:0%
one after the other.
-No way.

00:01:54.780 --> 00:01:56.449 line:0%
And then there was
a third movie after that.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:57.816 line:0%
I couldn't remember what it was.

00:01:57.816 --> 00:02:01.220 line:0%
-Was it called "Lenny"?
[ Ding! ]

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:06.258 line:0%
-Yes, it was "Lenny" --
it was the Lenny Bruce Story,

00:02:06.258 --> 00:02:07.894 line:0%
starring Dustin Hoffman.

00:02:07.894 --> 00:02:10.029 line:0%
That's --
-Yeah, not the things that --

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:13.832 line:0%
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:13.832 --> 00:02:15.301 line:0%
-It's exactly correct.

00:02:15.301 --> 00:02:16.769 line:0%
-That would be
"Mission: Impossible."

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.871 line:0%
Definitely.
-It definitely would be.

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:20.406 line:0%
But I was about to say,

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.609 line:0%
"One ticket for 'Notting Hill,'
please."

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:24.744 line:0%
And that's not what
the one they gave me.

00:02:24.744 --> 00:02:27.046 line:0%
They gave me a ticket
to a different film.

00:02:27.046 --> 00:02:28.581 line:0%
"Out of Africa"?
-[ Ding! ]

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:29.649 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
Yep.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.017 line:0%
That's where music started.

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:32.985 line:0%
That's where a cappella
music started.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:36.489 line:0%
And that's why they came up
with "Pitch Perfect."

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:39.192 line:0%
that song about
singing and a capella.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:41.093 line:0%
Of course. Of course.
And then, I mean,

00:02:41.093 --> 00:02:43.929 line:0%
if you're talking about
singing movies, you know,

00:02:43.929 --> 00:02:49.001 line:0%
and I guess
you'd have to mention, uh...

00:02:49.001 --> 00:02:51.403 line:0%
[ Both laugh ]

00:02:51.403 --> 00:02:53.706 line:0%
It's so easy.
So easy.

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:57.510 line:0%
-Uh, I'd just say "Queen,"
but that's not what it was.

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.545 line:0%
-It's not?
Sure it is.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:01.614 line:0%
[ Both laugh ]
-Is it?

00:03:01.614 --> 00:03:04.050 line:0%
-Yeah, well, I mean,
it was called "Queen."

00:03:04.050 --> 00:03:05.951 line:0%
What did you think
it was called?

00:03:05.951 --> 00:03:09.222 line:0%
"Rock 'n' Roll High School"?
[ Ding! ]

00:03:09.222 --> 00:03:12.558 line:0%
-Yeah, I mean...
Yeah, something like that.

00:03:12.558 --> 00:03:16.029 line:0%
But it certainly wasn't called
"Star Wars."

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:17.463 line:0%
We know that.
[ Ding! ]

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:21.700 line:0%
-Yeah, but that did not work
as I believe.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:25.505 line:0%
I think it went down
like the "Titanic."

00:03:25.505 --> 00:03:26.839 line:0%
-Yeah, it must have done --

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.209 line:0%
It must have gone
into the "Underworld."

00:03:29.209 --> 00:03:32.612 line:0%
-Yeah. Well, you know,
they came back to

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.847 line:0%
because, you know,
"V for Vendetta."

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.715 line:0%
You know,
they came back strong.

00:03:36.715 --> 00:03:39.585 line:0%
Ah, because that's absolutely --
Yeah.

00:03:39.585 --> 00:03:41.988 line:0%
But it was a wonder,
it was a wonder.

00:03:41.988 --> 00:03:43.655 line:0%
"Wonder Woman."
Yeah.

00:03:43.655 --> 00:03:45.624 line:0%
-She was.
She was a Wonder Woman,

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:49.228 line:0%
just like Olivia Newton-John
was in "Xanadu."

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:51.130 line:0%
[ Ding! ]
-In "Xanadu."

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.666 line:0%
That's right.
And...

00:03:53.666 --> 00:03:54.800 line:0%
-X?
-Yeah.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:56.168 line:0%
-Yeah, "Xanadu," right?

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:59.739 line:0%
Just a bunch of "Young Guns,"
basically, all of them.

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:03.009 line:0%
-They were once young.
"Young Guns."

00:04:03.009 --> 00:04:06.379 line:0%
-Yep. Young.
They certainly were young,

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:10.983 line:0%
young enough
to be a model in "Zoolander."

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:13.686 line:0%
-Yes!
-I love you, dude!

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.120 line:0%
I love you, man!

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:16.856 line:0%
My thanks to
Benedict Cumberbatch.

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:19.726 line:0%
His film, "The Courier,"
opens in theaters, March 19th.

